export default JSON.parse("{\"schema\":\"ai-brain-source-note/1.0\",\"domain\":\"studio-tools\",\"capabilities\":[\"3d\",\"brush\",\"class\",\"color\",\"effect\",\"generator\",\"grid\",\"layer\",\"lighting\",\"map\",\"merge\",\"paint\",\"settlement\",\"texture\",\"world\"],\"provenance\":{\"sourceGroup\":\"world-life-simulation-b\",\"sourceType\":\"provided-project-material\",\"archiveHash\":\"f54f3c537a009e3f\"},\"title\":\"readme.md\",\"content\":\"# Universal_3D_Visual_Studio\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nThis browser studio keeps the supplied Microsoft Paint / AddText-inspired shell and now provides two separate work modes inside the same interface:\\n\\n1. **3D Object** \u2014 import-only editing for already-made 3D objects.\\n2. **Stationary Map** \u2014 creation and editing of flat maps with optional non-destructive 3D relief, weather, lighting, water, and effect previews.\\n\\nThe map tools do not replace the Paint-style ribbon, palettes, brushes, AddText panel, classic sidebars, or retro window design. They are integrated into that same interface.\\n\\n## Start\\n\\nOpen `studio.html`. It is the only HTML file in the project. A local web server is recommended for the broadest model-decoder and browser compatibility, but common embedded GLB files and the map editor can also be opened directly in modern browsers.\\n\\n## 3D Object mode\\n\\n- Import existing GLB, glTF, OBJ, STL, FBX, DAE, 3MF, and AMF objects.\\n- Select existing meshes and material slots.\\n- Paint or erase directly on UV-mapped surfaces.\\n- Add 2D text and image stamps to object textures.\\n- Apply texture filters and programmed patterns.\\n- Add outline, glow, pulse, and Ichor Lightning effects.\\n- Export the edited object as GLB and active textures as PNG.\\n\\n### Object-mode guardrail\\n\\nObject editing remains import-only. There are no primitive generators, sculpting, extrusion, relief-mesh generation, image-to-mesh conversion, or standalone 3D-object creation tools. Auto UV adds texture coordinates to an imported mesh; it does not create a new object.\\n\\n## Stationary Map mode\\n\\n### Create or import maps\\n\\n- Start from parchment, paper, ocean, grass, stone, space, blank, or transparent surfaces.\\n- Import PNG, JPG, WEBP, and GIF stationary map images.\\n- Save and reopen editable `.belamap.json` map projects.\\n- Resize maps while preserving existing layers.\\n- Choose world/region, settlement/city, dungeon/interior, battlemap, or diagram workflows.\\n- Use no scale, 5-foot squares, 10-foot squares, one-mile, ten-mile, or 100-kilometer scale labels.\\n\\n### Paint-style map making\\n\\n- Layered raster editing with visibility, locking, opacity, blend modes, duplication, reordering, clearing, and merge-down.\\n- Terrain brushes for ocean, deep water, beach, grassland, forest, mountains, snow, desert, swamp, farmland, stone, caves, lava, and void/space.\\n- Paint, erase, eyedropper, line, rectangle, ellipse, road, river, wall, room, height, text, symbol, and effect-point tools.\\n- Square, hex, and dot grids with snapping and optional inclusion in exports.\\n- AddText-style labels with font, size, bold, italic, outline, shadow, rotation, opacity, and multiline placement.\\n- Map symbols for castles, cities, villages, towers, ruins, caves, camps, ports, bridges, ships, trees, mountains, stars, hazards, portals, temples, mines, and pins.\\n- Custom uploaded symbols and stamps.\\n- Compass rose, scale bar, decorative border, and legend-box helpers.\\n\\n### Map generators\\n\\n- Continent\\n- Archipelago\\n- Mountain ridge\\n- River system\\n- Connected dungeon rooms and corridors\\n- City blocks\\n- Forest scatter\\n- Coast roughening\\n\\nAll generated results are painted onto the active raster layer and remain editable with the same Paint-style tools.\\n\\n### Non-destructive 3D map effects\\n\\nThe map itself remains a stationary flat map. The 3D view is a preview layer and does not convert the map into a standalone mesh.\\n\\n- Paintable grayscale height map.\\n- Automatic height generation from terrain colors.\\n- Raise, lower, flatten, smooth, invert, and blur height operations.\\n- Relief-strength control.\\n- Water shimmer detected from blue map regions.\\n- Cloud layer, fog, rain, snow, embers, and fireflies.\\n- Day, golden-hour, night, moonlit, and storm lighting.\\n- Placeable glow, fire, magic, portal, and beacon effect points.\\n- Orbit, zoom, and pan preview controls.\\n- WebGL fallback message when hardware acceleration is unavailable; all 2D map functions and exports continue to work.\\n\\n### Map exports\\n\\n- PNG, JPG, and WEBP flat map images.\\n- Optional exported grid.\\n- Grayscale height-map PNG.\\n- 3D-preview screenshot.\\n- Editable `.belamap.json` project containing layers, height map, effects, grid settings, and markers.\\n- Backend metadata save with a reduced preview thumbnail.\\n\\n## Backend\\n\\n- Endpoint: `https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbxe3P6MBofPEhPfTAaz05TWEYhScX9QgpHzBKCdwPGnvzvVoyfllu0bAghZKqHs4E3hGg/exec`\\n- Apps Script library reference: `https://script.google.com/macros/library/d/1v06thwdjlv-j82hqHibJF3_gik7i8p9fFfK9nj0EOfi8VHhwT11jK5Eb/4`\\n\\nObject mode sends object-project metadata. Map mode sends map metadata, effect settings, grid settings, and a reduced thumbnail. Full-resolution local exports do not require the backend.\\n\\n## Source integration\\n\\nRelevant supplied repositories were used for map workflow, connected dungeon-layout concepts, VTT map organization, worldbuilding metadata, grid scales, browser project structure, Three.js rendering, and licensed map surface textures. See `map_source_references.json` and the notices in `licenses/`.\\n\"}");
